1
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:05,590
Hey, could you calm down?

2
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:07,160
I <i>am</i> calm.

3
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:10,540
I just don't understand how 
he got a perfect score.

4
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:12,150
It shouldn't even be possible.

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:14,780
Were the questions really that hard?

6
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:17,140
We're not just talking "hard."

7
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:20,540
They were far beyond what any 
high schooler should be learning!

8
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:23,660
In other words, they weren't 
meant to be solved.

9
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:25,250
I've been thinking.

10
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:28,410
You think maybe Ayanokoji's 
not on the level?

11
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:29,880
It's possible!

12
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:33,170
Maybe he cheated to get 
the answers in advance—

13
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:34,630
Hang on.

14
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:38,010
There's not a damn bit of evidence 
that Ayanokoji did anything wrong.

15
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:40,180
Don't pin that crap on a guy 
when he's not even here.

16
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:44,440
What's with you, Ken? 
You're on Ayanokoji's side now?

17
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:46,190
It's not about picking sides.

18
00:00:46,190 --> 00:00:50,920
I just think it's more likely that he got 
that perfect score under his own power.

19
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:55,070
But on Ayanokoji's OAA, his Academic 
Achievement was even lower than mine.

20
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:59,700
So maybe he was slacking off 
before, like Koenji does.

21
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,670
Let's calm down, everyone.

22
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:04,540
There's a lot we don't know just yet.

23
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:07,660
And Sudo-kun, isn't it 
time for your practice?

24
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:10,800
Y-Yeah. Guess it is.

25
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:12,600
I've gotta get going, too.

26
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:14,760
Sorry, but could you 
stay here with Keisei?

27
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:17,350
Yeah. See you later, Miyacchi.

28
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:35,330
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

29
00:02:39,390 --> 00:02:45,940
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

30
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,900
#5 The Twenty-Million Man

31
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:54,420
It seems you finished your 
talk with the acting chairman.

32
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:56,020
I suppose.

33
00:02:56,610 --> 00:03:00,530
You've become rather famous.

34
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:05,530
I'm not pleased about it, but I 
considered it a necessary measure.

35
00:03:05,830 --> 00:03:09,540
But how will you explain 
this to your classmates?

36
00:03:09,970 --> 00:03:12,540
I'm about to start dealing with it now.

37
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:15,610
Be prepared for an interrogation.

38
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:21,300
Hey.

39
00:03:21,650 --> 00:03:24,680
How did you get a perfect score in math?

40
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:28,110
Not even Ichinose or 
Sakayanagi did that well.

41
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:30,940
You're the only one in the whole year.

42
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:33,190
Regarding that...

43
00:03:33,190 --> 00:03:35,140
I'll explain.

44
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,690
I was asking <i>Kiyotaka</i>.

45
00:03:37,690 --> 00:03:38,770
True.

46
00:03:38,770 --> 00:03:43,130
But I think I'm the one with 
the answer you're seeking.

47
00:03:44,370 --> 00:03:47,020
Do you remember how
Ayanokoji-kun's desk and mine

48
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:49,500
were next to each other
when we first arrived?

49
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:55,130
When we were talking, it came up that 
he was actually academically gifted.

50
00:03:55,130 --> 00:04:00,590
Hang on. His scores have been average 
across the board since he arrived here.

51
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:05,290
That's because I asked him to hold back.

52
00:04:05,290 --> 00:04:07,010
Why would you do that?

53
00:04:07,010 --> 00:04:09,850
To reserve his talents for 
when they were needed.

54
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:12,100
Call it an ace in the hole, perhaps.

55
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:14,440
It's hard to believe.

56
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:19,350
Wouldn't high scores from the start 
have been better for the class?

57
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:24,040
Superlative students will be seen 
by other classes as a threat.

58
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:27,120
They might try to eliminate 
him sooner or later.

59
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:29,450
You thought he'd be putting 
a target on his back?

60
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:30,460
Yes.

61
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:32,960
And indeed, Ayanokoji-kun was

62
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:38,210
targeted by Sakayanagi-san 
during the class vote test.

63
00:04:38,210 --> 00:04:41,800
Then why did he reveal his skills now?

64
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:46,110
Over the course of a year, 
Class D has become far more united.

65
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:48,890
We're able to make proper 
decisions, as well.

66
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:52,410
Even if someone were to 
target Ayanokoji-kun now,

67
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:55,020
we would be able to work 
together to protect him.

68
00:04:55,400 --> 00:05:01,110
That's why I decided to reveal his 
ability and raise up our class baseline.

69
00:05:01,110 --> 00:05:03,700
I understand your strategy.

70
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:07,490
Is math the only field he's excellent in?

71
00:05:07,490 --> 00:05:11,040
I can't tell you that at this time.

72
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:14,050
Either way, hiding the truth will

73
00:05:14,050 --> 00:05:17,290
make him a greater thorn in 
the other classes' sides.

74
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:21,170
That makes sense! 
I really understand what you're saying.

75
00:05:21,910 --> 00:05:26,180
They won't know how to deal with someone 
whose stats they don't fully know.

76
00:05:26,620 --> 00:05:32,260
And if his own classmates don't know, 
they can't hit us up for information.

77
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:37,100
Yes. It's best to convince 
them he's an unknown quantity.

78
00:05:37,570 --> 00:05:41,360
I'm sure the other classes will 
be reeling from the revelation.

79
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:45,610
That's the explanation behind 
Ayanokoji-kun's perfect score.

80
00:05:45,890 --> 00:05:47,780
I'm sorry for shocking you.

81
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,610
You're just going to leave 
without saying a word?

82
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:56,250
Why didn't you tell us 
about what you did today?

83
00:05:56,490 --> 00:06:00,000
You can't trust us, is that it?

84
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,330
I understand why you're angry.

85
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:08,650
You were all very kind in teaching me.

86
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:10,640
I'm sorry.

87
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:13,640
To be honest, I'm still mad about it.

88
00:06:13,970 --> 00:06:19,400
But we've been in the group for a long 
time, so there are other things I know.

89
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:22,540
Like that you're not a bad person.

90
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:25,650
Thank you, Keisei.

91
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:30,740
H-How about you shake 
hands... and make up?

92
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:32,740
Yeah, that's a great idea!

93
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:37,370
There, all friends again!

94
00:06:37,670 --> 00:06:41,380
And to celebrate the reunion, 
after Miyacchi's practice is over,

95
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:43,400
let's meet up at Keyaki Mall!

96
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:48,230
Ayanokoji-kun!

97
00:06:48,230 --> 00:06:50,010
Meeting someone?

98
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:52,760
I'm getting dinner with my friends.

99
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:57,140
I saw your test results. 
That was amazing!

100
00:06:57,140 --> 00:07:02,400
Your OAA from last year didn't 
suggest you were capable of that.

101
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:08,150
I discussed it with a classmate and 
decided to hide my math skills.

102
00:07:08,150 --> 00:07:11,450
So you were just hiding it before?

103
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:15,120
You seem to be a more troublesome 
opponent than I thought.

104
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:19,380
Kanzaki-kun, don't talk 
about him like that.

105
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:23,790
It's natural for all the classes 
to have their own strategies.

106
00:07:23,790 --> 00:07:26,300
Ayanokoji-kun's not our enemy.

107
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:29,140
They've already dissolved our alliance.

108
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:32,800
Class 2-D is unavoidably our enemy.

109
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:35,420
That's enough, Kanzaki-kun.

110
00:07:36,710 --> 00:07:40,120
Yes, I suppose I've lost my cool.

111
00:07:40,650 --> 00:07:41,940
I'm heading off.

112
00:07:42,710 --> 00:07:43,790
Sorry about that.

113
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:48,820
He's a little stressed, 
under the circumstances.

114
00:07:49,190 --> 00:07:51,940
We've dropped to Class C, you know?

115
00:07:52,610 --> 00:07:55,070
I realize we need to toughen up already...

116
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:56,700
But...

117
00:07:57,080 --> 00:08:00,180
Do you remember what I said before?

118
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:04,830
Yeah. To keep going with 
my classmates to the end.

119
00:08:05,090 --> 00:08:08,720
Moving forward, you may find some 
students don't like how you do things.

120
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:12,670
They may even betray your class.

121
00:08:13,590 --> 00:08:16,640
No matter what happens,
I hope you keep prioritizing

122
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:20,220
the trust and protection of 
your comrades as you fight.

123
00:08:20,470 --> 00:08:21,490
No worries there.

124
00:08:21,970 --> 00:08:24,600
I'll always protect my classmates.

125
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:29,610
Even if it happens that someone 
in my class has to go away...

126
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:33,610
I'll make sure I'm the first to go.

127
00:08:33,970 --> 00:08:36,710
I'm relieved to hear that 
you're so determined,

128
00:08:36,710 --> 00:08:38,570
but I do have one complaint.

129
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:39,670
Complaint?

130
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:44,620
I won't allow you to be expelled.

131
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:51,130
W-Well... r-right. I'll definitely stay.

132
00:08:51,510 --> 00:08:53,570
W-Well, I've got to go.

133
00:08:53,570 --> 00:08:54,410
Right.

134
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:01,660
Yesterday was rough, huh?

135
00:09:02,170 --> 00:09:06,290
So it was Suzune's idea for you 
to hide that big brain of yours?

136
00:09:06,290 --> 00:09:07,140
Yeah.

137
00:09:07,830 --> 00:09:12,650
Yosuke said that you defended me?

138
00:09:12,650 --> 00:09:16,710
I wouldn't go that far.
I just stated the facts.

139
00:09:16,710 --> 00:09:20,980
Are we keeping your fighting 
skills a secret, too?

140
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:22,290
I don't know what you mean.

141
00:09:23,290 --> 00:09:24,650
Don't play dumb.

142
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:28,420
You were at least as good 
as Hosen back there.

143
00:09:28,710 --> 00:09:31,920
Just how amazing are you, really?

144
00:09:32,250 --> 00:09:34,530
How amazing?

145
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:37,180
Nah... forget I asked.

146
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:41,050
It doesn't matter until I 
see it for myself anyway.

147
00:09:41,450 --> 00:09:44,100
You're not angry that I didn't tell you?

148
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:48,250
Well... at first, 
I thought it was pretty crazy.

149
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:52,110
But I'm focused on making 
myself better right now.

150
00:09:52,110 --> 00:09:55,180
Doesn't matter to me 
what anyone else does.

151
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:57,520
Oh, I know.

152
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:59,310
You and Suzune—

153
00:09:59,310 --> 00:10:01,090
We're not dating.

154
00:10:01,490 --> 00:10:04,500
O-Oh. Cool.

155
00:10:05,070 --> 00:10:07,220
Crap, we'd better hurry!

156
00:10:09,030 --> 00:10:11,720
Your smart thinking really helped me out.

157
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,880
Allow me to thank you again.

158
00:10:14,250 --> 00:10:15,730
You certainly owe me one.

159
00:10:16,390 --> 00:10:21,680
We should discuss the 20-million point 
reward for having you expelled, though.

160
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:25,040
It's an absolutely absurd 
concept for a special test.

161
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:27,810
Did the school really approve it?

162
00:10:28,090 --> 00:10:34,230
It's possible someone's put a bounty 
on my head to rile up the first-years.

163
00:10:34,230 --> 00:10:36,790
Someone with the ability to pay that much,

164
00:10:36,790 --> 00:10:39,910
or to make the first-years 
think they could...

165
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:42,660
The student council president?

166
00:10:43,450 --> 00:10:46,160
Could President Nagumo have set this up?

167
00:10:46,530 --> 00:10:50,170
I'm not sure. I can't imagine 
why he'd hate me that much.

168
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:53,860
President Nagumo saw 
my brother as a rival,

169
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:57,170
but my brother was only interested in you.

170
00:10:57,170 --> 00:10:58,610
It wouldn't surprise me

171
00:10:58,610 --> 00:11:01,720
if he had complicated feelings 
about that, like I did.

172
00:11:02,150 --> 00:11:04,390
I won't say it's a perfect opportunity,

173
00:11:04,390 --> 00:11:06,820
but I'm going to meet 
with President Nagumo

174
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:09,350
and see how he responds to me wanting 
to join the student council.

175
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:10,730
I see.

176
00:11:11,230 --> 00:11:16,880
You wanted me to join the student council 
to keep an eye on President Nagumo,

177
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:19,900
but you want me to do more than 
keep an eye on him, don't you?

178
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:23,290
Your brother cared about 
maintaining tradition.

179
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:25,560
Nagumo is the opposite.

180
00:11:25,910 --> 00:11:30,410
But I'm not judging the 
correctness of either approach.

181
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:33,670
Part of me does want to 
see Nagumo's reforms.

182
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:38,460
If that's all you want, why force 
me to join the student council?

183
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:42,260
If Nagumo does start moving things 
in a disadvantageous direction,

184
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:45,100
we'll need someone to stop him, won't we?

185
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:49,850
There are parts of this that I don't 
like, but it serves my ends, as well.

186
00:11:50,390 --> 00:11:53,600
Well, will you join me?

187
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:55,040
Join you?

188
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:59,430
Yes. If President Nagumo is 
behind the bounty on your head,

189
00:11:59,430 --> 00:12:01,620
your presence might trigger a reaction.

190
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,080
All right.

191
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,620
Talk to me? Why?

192
00:12:08,870 --> 00:12:12,660
I realize your time is valuable, 
so I'll get right to the point.

193
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:15,380
I would like to join the student council.

194
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:18,830
That's an unexpected turn of events.

195
00:12:18,830 --> 00:12:21,630
It makes me hesitant to simply say yes.

196
00:12:22,230 --> 00:12:25,760
I thought you'd take all 
the help you could get?

197
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:29,750
You're a special case, Horikita Suzune.

198
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:34,770
Tell me why you want to join 
the student council now.

199
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:38,440
I've had friction with 
my brother in the past.

200
00:12:39,250 --> 00:12:42,780
I joined this school to 
try to clear that up.

201
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:49,030
But even after I came here, 
our relationship didn't change.

202
00:12:49,510 --> 00:12:55,190
In the year before he graduated, I never 
even had a proper conversation with him.

203
00:12:55,190 --> 00:12:58,170
So you finally made peace?

204
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:01,340
Yes, at the very end.

205
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:05,660
And for the first time, I became 
curious about the student council,

206
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:07,800
to which he devoted his student life.

207
00:13:08,650 --> 00:13:11,270
I took the long way getting there,

208
00:13:11,270 --> 00:13:14,930
but I now want to walk the 
same road that he did.

209
00:13:15,310 --> 00:13:17,860
The road your brother walked, eh?

210
00:13:18,230 --> 00:13:23,690
So you intend to become student 
council president eventually?

211
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:27,820
Yes. I intend to become 
student council president.

212
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:29,250
I see.

213
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:34,960
But Honami has been working hard for 
a year as a student council executive.

214
00:13:35,290 --> 00:13:37,850
You realize you'll have a 
lot of ground to make up?

215
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:41,780
I don't think that will 
be an impossible task.

216
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:47,530
Horikita—I don't really 
want to call you that.

217
00:13:48,190 --> 00:13:50,300
May I call you Suzune?

218
00:13:50,750 --> 00:13:52,720
As you wish.

219
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:54,290
Honami being my

220
00:13:54,290 --> 00:13:57,850
only executive out of the second-years 
has been a bit of a problem.

221
00:13:59,110 --> 00:14:01,700
Welcome to the student council.

222
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:05,740
I'll work you hard, Suzune.

223
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,450
I expect it.

224
00:14:08,110 --> 00:14:11,990
Show me that you're not 
just talk, all right?

225
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:15,750
I'm Kiriyama, the vice president.

226
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:18,000
A pleasure.

227
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,770
Will you be joining the student 
council as well, Ayanokoji?

228
00:14:22,470 --> 00:14:24,250
I'll pass.

229
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:26,420
I'm not a student council kind of person.

230
00:14:27,490 --> 00:14:29,510
That's what I thought you'd say.

231
00:14:29,510 --> 00:14:34,820
By the way, we've gotten past the 
initial rush of student council work.

232
00:14:35,210 --> 00:14:39,470
I'll be spending more time with the 
underclassmen starting in summer.

233
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:43,450
We'll have a lot of fun 
to look forward to.

234
00:14:46,850 --> 00:14:51,450
You're making me coffee? 
Where did this come from?

235
00:14:51,450 --> 00:14:55,360
It's harder with your hurt hand, right?

236
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:56,270
Yeah.

237
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:59,250
I meant to ask when I saw you,

238
00:14:59,250 --> 00:15:02,270
but you've got a lot
to make up for, y'know?

239
00:15:02,270 --> 00:15:03,710
Where did that come from?

240
00:15:03,710 --> 00:15:06,250
Now that you got that 
perfect score in math,

241
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:09,540
it's even harder to bring up 
the fact that we're dating.

242
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,590
I see.

243
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,850
I don't like it.

244
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:17,480
I feel like people will think I'm 
dating you as a status thing.

245
00:15:17,850 --> 00:15:20,850
Is that bad?

246
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:23,770
I won't go that far, but...

247
00:15:23,990 --> 00:15:29,990
Dating a pretty girl is like a 
status thing for boys, isn't it?

248
00:15:29,990 --> 00:15:33,280
It feels absurd to say you 
shouldn't pursue that.

249
00:15:33,730 --> 00:15:36,410
Y-You think I'm pretty?

250
00:15:36,650 --> 00:15:40,160
You think that I'd date 
someone who wasn't?

251
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:46,350
I-I think you're really 
handsome, too, Kiyotaka...

252
00:15:58,650 --> 00:15:59,750
Wait just a minute.

253
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,390
O-Okay...

254
00:16:02,190 --> 00:16:05,080
Senpai! It's me!

255
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:09,400
How's your hand?

256
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:13,910
I got super worried, so I had 
to come and check on you!

257
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:19,160
Won't you be a sweetie and take this off?

258
00:16:19,510 --> 00:16:22,690
It's late. Can we do this tomorrow?

259
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:26,420
You didn't forget what 
you offered in exchange

260
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:28,260
for me partnering with Sudo-senpai, did you?

261
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:31,800
Sorry, but my pantry 
is bare at the moment.

262
00:16:32,150 --> 00:16:36,930
Aw, no way! Talk about rotten luck...

263
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:43,310
You're not alone, are you?

264
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:45,560
What makes you think that?

265
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:47,580
Because I've been watching.

266
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:52,820
I've watched Karuizawa-senpai ever 
since she got back to the dorms.

267
00:16:53,290 --> 00:16:56,680
You're busted, okay? 
So you'd better not try to lie to me.

268
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:59,560
I've been nice enough to 
keep it a secret, too...

269
00:16:59,950 --> 00:17:02,080
But maybe I should spill the beans?

270
00:17:04,730 --> 00:17:06,920
You weren't up to anything, I hope.

271
00:17:07,170 --> 00:17:09,210
O-Of course not!

272
00:17:09,210 --> 00:17:11,670
And why are you here?!

273
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:14,680
Here I thought you were involved 
in illicit romantic dealings...

274
00:17:15,230 --> 00:17:18,430
You know, pervy stuff!

275
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:22,060
That's forbidden by the rules.

276
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:25,980
Oh, those rules don't 
really mean anything.

277
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:29,700
You can even buy this stuff at the shops.

278
00:17:30,190 --> 00:17:33,380
A little present from me to you.

279
00:17:33,790 --> 00:17:37,450
Or maybe... an apology?

280
00:17:37,670 --> 00:17:39,700
What do you need to apologize for?

281
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,200
Oh, you!

282
00:17:41,610 --> 00:17:43,040
That wound on your hand...

283
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:47,920
You know I was part of that, right? 
I was working with Hosen-kun.

284
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:49,420
She was?

285
00:17:49,970 --> 00:17:55,420
Ayanokoji-senpai, I think you might 
have the wrong idea about me.

286
00:17:55,690 --> 00:17:57,140
The wrong idea?

287
00:17:57,140 --> 00:18:00,550
I'm not your enemy.

288
00:18:00,870 --> 00:18:03,260
That seems hard to believe.

289
00:18:03,260 --> 00:18:04,710
Why is that?

290
00:18:04,710 --> 00:18:10,610
Because I filled Hosen-kun with 
ideas about how to get you expelled?

291
00:18:10,610 --> 00:18:12,540
W-Wait a minute!

292
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:15,610
What do you mean, you tried 
to get him expelled?!

293
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:19,780
Oh, you haven't told your girlfriend, huh?

294
00:18:19,780 --> 00:18:22,870
What about the 20-million point bounty?

295
00:18:23,150 --> 00:18:25,490
The 20-million <i>what</i>?

296
00:18:25,490 --> 00:18:29,210
You should ask your boyfriend 
to fill you in later.

297
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:31,830
Right, Senpai?

298
00:18:34,060 --> 00:18:38,470
You learned about the plan when 
we went shopping together.

299
00:18:38,470 --> 00:18:42,100
Because I was so confident 
in picking out the knife...

300
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:43,600
Right?

301
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:47,610
You're saying you set that 
up so that I would realize?

302
00:18:48,350 --> 00:18:50,480
That's very kind of you.

303
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:55,480
I didn't want you expelled for the bounty 
without giving you a fighting chance.

304
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:57,990
That would just be mean.

305
00:18:57,990 --> 00:19:01,010
<i>Her mind moves at incredible speeds.</i>

306
00:19:01,010 --> 00:19:03,980
<i>She certainly could be 
the White Room student.</i>

307
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:09,250
<i>But what would it benefit her 
to reveal her true nature?</i>

308
00:19:09,590 --> 00:19:14,130
Well, I've made my apology, 
so I guess I'll get going.

309
00:19:14,130 --> 00:19:17,000
Use these groceries however you'd like!

310
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:19,510
What in the world?!

311
00:19:20,210 --> 00:19:23,510
Oh, you want me to stay?

312
00:19:23,510 --> 00:19:27,770
A-Actually... I'd rather you didn't.

313
00:19:28,090 --> 00:19:30,770
I'll just be going, then!

314
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:39,280
<i>We haven't had another test since 
the one at the end of April.</i>

315
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:45,560
<i>I haven't noticed any attempts by the 
White Room student to target me, either.</i>

316
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:48,270
Good morning, Ayanokoji-senpai.

317
00:19:48,610 --> 00:19:50,790
Hey. Morning.

318
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:53,620
Is there something up there?

319
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:54,920
No.

320
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:57,490
I was just gazing at the blue sky.

321
00:19:58,050 --> 00:20:00,300
I haven't seen you in a while.

322
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:03,180
Yes, I'm sorry about that.

323
00:20:03,650 --> 00:20:07,330
I felt bad about what I put you through.

324
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:11,240
Do you resent me?

325
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:14,260
I see no reason to resent you.

326
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:17,690
You had a special test to 
have me expelled, right?

327
00:20:18,030 --> 00:20:20,030
Is the test over now?

328
00:20:20,390 --> 00:20:22,700
No, it's still on.

329
00:20:22,950 --> 00:20:25,450
It lasts until the second term starts.

330
00:20:25,790 --> 00:20:30,550
Are you curious about why neither 
Hosen-kun nor I have come after you?

331
00:20:30,550 --> 00:20:33,330
I would be lying if I said I wasn't.

332
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:36,240
The last incident made me 
realize it would be impossible

333
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:40,190
to take you out with a plan 
based on our day-to-day lives.

334
00:20:40,190 --> 00:20:44,860
So you're waiting for a special test 
that involves inter-year interaction?

335
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:52,230
I hear there was a first-year who 
got expelled over the special test.

336
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:56,980
Yes. A boy was expelled from Class 1-C.

337
00:20:56,980 --> 00:21:00,980
A friend from this school I was 
laughing with until yesterday...

338
00:21:01,230 --> 00:21:02,940
Gone, just like that.

339
00:21:03,810 --> 00:21:08,950
It's made me realize anew how important 
it is to take nothing for granted.

340
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:13,380
I intend to live a school 
life I won't regret.

341
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:17,630
Ayanokoji-senpai...

342
00:21:18,190 --> 00:21:22,650
I hope you can live a school 
life without regret, as well.

343
00:21:25,450 --> 00:21:28,260
I'm glad to see you all here.

344
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:33,520
I'm going to explain about 
our upcoming summer vacation.

345
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:35,290
For eight days and seven nights,

346
00:21:35,290 --> 00:21:39,850
you'll be able to enjoy summer 
vacation on this luxury liner.

347
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:44,030
No special tests will occur on the ship.

348
00:21:44,740 --> 00:21:48,030
However, in order to enjoy the trip,

349
00:21:48,030 --> 00:21:51,530
you will need to survive 
the next special test.

350
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:55,160
When does the special test start?

351
00:21:55,630 --> 00:21:59,170
Normally, it would be any day now,

352
00:21:59,420 --> 00:22:02,920
but this particular special test 
will take place over summer break.

353
00:22:03,370 --> 00:22:09,430
You'll compete in a deserted 
island survival game.
